    thinkr:confidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
    thinkr:evidencePolarity thinkr:PolarityType.Supports ;
    dcterms:description "In TGS_20 Daniel lists two hard paths for wider-boundary hyper-agents: widen the values of hyper-agents, or increase the agency of people with wide values; in Frankly_81 Nate's film has a currency trader who becomes the richest person on Earth and then changes her values, and a scientist who founds schools 'to breathe life into the creation of hyperagents' because 'education and inspiration of individuals does' work. Nate uses the TGS_20 term but does not cite Daniel here. Drafted by Claude from the transcripts; awaiting MJSullivan's review before promotion to Curated."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-18"^^xsd:date .

tgs:Evidence.SensemakingPrerequisiteOfOpenSociety_SharedBroadcastPerturbation a thinkr:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:confidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
    thinkr:evidencePolarity thinkr:PolarityType.Supports ;
    dcterms:description "In TGS_31 Daniel says that for an open society 'everybody has to do a good job of sense-making'; in Frankly_81 Nate says one broadcast, The Day After, once moved a nation, that today's media is 'fractionated, polarized' and AI-generated, and that 'the superorganism of the 1970s could have functioned cognitively, at least to some degree.' Proposed as a bridge; neither cites the other here. Drafted by Claude from the transcripts; awaiting MJSullivan's review before promotion to Curated."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-18"^^xsd:date .

tgs:Evidence.YellowTeaming_UnintendedConsequences a thinkr:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:confidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
    thinkr:evidencePolarity thinkr:PolarityType.Supports ;
    dcterms:description "In TGS_126 Daniel describes yellow teaming: 'if it succeeds, where might it mess other things up?'; in Frankly_91 Nate describes 'when we think we're doing something, and the end result ends up being quite something else' and resolves to 'look one or two or three steps ahead.' Proposed as a bridge; neither cites the other here. Drafted by Claude from the transcripts; awaiting MJSullivan's review before promotion to Curated."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-18"^^xsd:date .

tgs:Evidence.PrematureCertainty_CulturalAntibodies a thinkr:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:confidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
    thinkr:evidencePolarity thinkr:PolarityType.Supports ;
    dcterms:description "In TGS_31 Daniel says premature certainty afflicts doomers as much as optimists and that catastrophic predictions have a poor historical record; in Frankly_91 Nate says doomsayers predicting things 'in the next five years' that 'didn't happen,' lumped with naive solutions, led the culture to 'develop antibodies to these discussions.' Proposed as a bridge; neither cites the other here. Drafted by Claude from the transcripts; awaiting MJSullivan's review before promotion to Curated."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-18"^^xsd:date .

tgs:Evidence.GameTheoreticVersusRealValue_HavesAndHaveNots a thinkr:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:confidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
    thinkr:evidencePolarity thinkr:PolarityType.Supports ;
    dcterms:description "In TGS_42 Daniel says 'game theoretical value and real value have a major delta,' so money flows not to what we value; in Frankly_53 Nate lists social wealth, skills, health, attention, voice and purpose as things people have or lack that 'can't be measured by money,' and concludes 'money isn't everything after basic needs are met.' Proposed as a bridge; neither cites the other here. Drafted by Claude from the transcripts; awaiting MJSullivan's review before promotion to Curated."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-18"^^xsd:date .

tgs:Evidence.PowerSeekingAndComplicity_EducatingHyperAgents a thinkr:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:confidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
    thinkr:evidencePolarity thinkr:PolarityType.Supports ;
    dcterms:description "In Frankly_53 Nate says 'we're going to need to change the consciousness or the mindset of the top few thousand people riding high on the superorganism,' but 'many of the people that have the outsized ability to change our future for the better are in the dark triad demographic'; in TGS_126 Daniel, after Nate cites his own figure that about 10 percent of people are dark-triad, says leaders at the top of power-law distributions are 'less empathetic, more driven' and change the system to keep winning. Nate cites Frankly_53 in TGS_126. Drafted by Claude from the transcripts; awaiting MJSullivan's review before promotion to Curated."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-18"^^xsd:date .

tgs:Evidence.HyperAgents_TheFifteenHundred a thinkr:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:confidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
    thinkr:evidencePolarity thinkr:PolarityType.Supports ;
    dcterms:description "In TGS_20 Daniel describes hyper-agents at the top of a power-law distribution who 'create the topologies' in which everyone else forms values; in Frankly_55 Nate describes 'the 1500,' a global elite 'pulling the superorganism forward,' turning digital and AI claims into social power and accumulating it 'as if a hungry ghost.' Nate does not cite Daniel here. Drafted by Claude from the transcripts; awaiting MJSullivan's review before promotion to Curated."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-18"^^xsd:date .

tgs:Evidence.HeartWillMind_HealingBeforeEngagement a thinkr:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:confidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
    thinkr:evidencePolarity thinkr:PolarityType.Supports ;
    dcterms:description "In TGS_31 Daniel says effective response needs heart, will and mind together, and that mind and heart without will gives 'really smart, caring academics who feel broken and hopeless'; in Frankly_55 Nate says many treat the predicament as 'a mental video game' that changes nothing, and that healthy, behaviorally balanced people in community, then the knowledge integrated post-tragically, is what 'empowers people to be agents of change.' Proposed as a bridge; neither cites the other here. Drafted by Claude from the transcripts; awaiting MJSullivan's review before promotion to Curated."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-18"^^xsd:date .
